{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"salted-growable-murrelet","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# Hard-remove the deprecated `resolved_statuses` config keys\n\nFollow-up to task [rebar:549c-032f-6cb0-4258], which decided DEPRECATE-not-remove and executed\nthe deprecation half. This ticket is the removal half, and it is deliberately BLOCKED ON\nOPERATOR SIGN-OFF because removing a documented, operator-facing config key is a user-visible\nsurface change.\n\n## Why this was not done inline\n\n549c established that `jira.resolved_statuses` was live and behaviour-affecting as recently as\nshipped tag v0.10.1 (the inbound absence probe was reachable then and\n`adapters/jira/probe.py::_resolve_resolved_statuses` read the key), and that the pre-f020 docs\nactively instructed self-hosted operators to set it. So real `pyproject.toml`s in the wild\nplausibly carry it.\n\nThe project's precedent for retiring a zero-read-site operator-facing key — `code_health.enabled`,\n`reconciler.lock_backend`, `reconciler.lock_max_retries` — is to delete the schema field and add\na warn-class tombstone, so existing config keeps loading with a warning instead of erroring.\nThat precedent was applied \"per the operator ruling\" on bug a573-00ea-2bf6-4eb1, i.e. sign-off\ncame first. 549c had no such ruling, so it stopped at the deprecation.\n\n## What to do once sign-off is obtained\n\n* Delete `JiraConfig.resolved_statuses` and `ReconcilerConfig.resolved_statuses` from\n  `src/rebar/_config_schema.py`, plus their `_as_str_list` coercer entries.\n* Add warn-class tombstones `_tomb(\"cfg\", \"jira.resolved_statuses\", \"\", \"warn\")` and\n  `_tomb(\"cfg\", \"reconciler.resolved_statuses\", \"\", \"warn\")` in `src/rebar/_deprecations.py`,\n  and drop the two `_scheduled` deprecation rows 549c added.\n* Tombstone the auto-derived env twins if they exist (`REBAR_JIRA_RESOLVED_STATUSES`,\n  `REBAR_RECONCILER_RESOLVED_STATUSES`), following the `REBAR_CODE_HEALTH_ENABLED` precedent.\n* Remove the two `# read-via:` markers (they point at this ticket) and update\n  `tests/scripts/test_check_config_reads_heldout.py` accordingly.\n* Remove both keys from `docs/config.md` and `docs/user-guide.md`.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] operator sign-off for the removal is recorded on this ticket\n- [ ] both schema fields and their coercers are deleted\n- [ ] both keys are tombstoned warn-class, so an existing config still loads with a warning\n- [ ] the `# read-via:` markers are gone and the heldout marker test matches\n- [ ] neither key is documented any more\n- [ ] `make lint`, `make typecheck`, `make test` green; `Verified +1` before close","id":"f408-64ad-ee41-46b6","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Remove the deprecated resolved_statuses config keys (needs operator sign-off)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786559177022131001,"uuid":"c4f42daf-160c-410f-9ead-324c03ab11ca"}